   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I would like to remove the too much white space between bars of the attached bar plot.   But, I could not remove this.  I followed several solutions posted on stack overflow and in this google forum as well- nothing worked.  My graph is generated from metagenomics data.  Here&#39;s the code I originally used to generate this graph:</div><div><br></div><div>ggplot(data = psmelt(ps.taxa_rarefy_control_CR_JAX_TAC_hi_abundant), mapping = aes_string(x = &quot;vendor&quot;, y = &quot;Abundance&quot;)) + </div><div>  geom_bar(aes(color=Family, fill=Family), stat=&quot;identity&quot;, position=&quot;fill&quot;, width = 0.2) + theme_bw() + </div><div>  theme(panel.border = element_blank(), panel.grid.major = element_blank(), panel.grid.minor = element_blank(), axis.line = element_line(colour = &quot;black&quot;), legend.position = &quot;bottom&quot;) + xlab(&quot;   &quot;) +</div><div>  guides(color = guide_legend(nrow=6)) +</div><div>  scale_x_discrete(expand = c(0, 0))<br></div><div>  </div><div>I will greatly appreciate if you please let me know how can I remove the space between CR, JAX and TAC bars.   I also tried the binwidth=0 within ggplot function, but it didn&#39;t work.</div><div><br></div><div><br>Thanks,</div><div><br>Saif</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
